1
00:01:41,324 --> 00:01:44,828
All right! Easy... Whoa... okay, okay!

2
00:01:45,528 --> 00:01:46,529
Got it...

3
00:01:48,164 --> 00:01:51,034
Excuse me. I got lost.

4
00:01:51,868 --> 00:01:53,703
I'm busy right now. Ask me later.

5
00:01:53,937 --> 00:01:57,540
Ryo-chan, how can you say that? Just tell him the way.

6
00:01:58,508 --> 00:02:01,177
Ouch! What are you doing?

7
00:02:01,377 --> 00:02:03,179
Bah! Game over!

8
00:02:03,380 --> 00:02:04,214
What is it?

9
00:02:04,547 --> 00:02:06,216
Can I borrow a map?

10
00:02:06,416 --> 00:02:08,518
Here, find it yourself.

11
00:02:09,352 --> 00:02:10,954
What year is this map from?

12
00:02:11,388 --> 00:02:13,223
No idea.

13
00:02:13,423 --> 00:02:15,325
It's the latest edition published this year.

14
00:02:16,359 --> 00:02:17,193
Thank you.

15
00:02:17,394 --> 00:02:18,161
You're welcome.

16
00:02:18,361 --> 00:02:21,164
Officer Nakagawa, reporting back from patrol.

17
00:02:21,364 --> 00:02:22,565
Good work.

18
00:02:22,866 --> 00:02:26,836
I see. This river has been filled in and turned into a road.

19
00:02:27,604 --> 00:02:28,838
No wonder I got lost.

20
00:02:29,372 --> 00:02:32,208
Okay, I'll update the data in my navigation system.

21
00:02:32,609 --> 00:02:35,612
A navigation system? Do you have one?

22
00:02:36,279 --> 00:02:38,615
Yes. May I borrow your desk for a second?

23
00:02:38,848 --> 00:02:40,183
Oh, sure...

24
00:02:44,921 --> 00:02:45,588
Oh!

25
00:02:45,989 --> 00:02:48,057
It has a built-in computer.

26
00:02:48,258 --> 00:02:50,994
Wow, where's the keyboard?

27
00:02:51,628 --> 00:02:52,295
An abacus?

28
00:02:52,562 --> 00:02:54,631
It doesn't seem like just an ordinary abacus.

29
00:02:55,465 --> 00:02:56,933
Oh, I see.

30
00:03:00,403 --> 00:03:01,237
Hmm...

31
00:03:01,571 --> 00:03:04,107
Wow, he's so quick!

32
00:03:04,607 --> 00:03:05,308
Ah!

33
00:03:05,708 --> 00:03:07,277
Hmm? Wow!

34
00:03:11,548 --> 00:03:13,550
The abacus is the keyboard!

35
00:03:16,586 --> 00:03:17,787
Update completed.

36
00:03:18,188 --> 00:03:20,457
This is amazing!

37
00:03:20,657 --> 00:03:21,624
I'll save it.

38
00:03:21,858 --> 00:03:23,560
It's pretty cool.

39
00:03:23,760 --> 00:03:25,762
-It's one o'clock. Time for cram school. -Wow.

40
00:03:25,962 --> 00:03:29,265
Amazing! It even manages your schedule.

41
00:03:29,499 --> 00:03:31,267
On no. I won't make it to cram school.

42
00:03:31,468 --> 00:03:33,470
I'll just fax over my homework.

43
00:03:34,237 --> 00:03:35,338
Oh, if you need a fax—

44
00:03:35,572 --> 00:03:36,473
Don't worry.

45
00:03:36,673 --> 00:03:37,340
Eh?

46
00:03:39,909 --> 00:03:41,644
What? It even has a fax machine?

47
00:03:41,878 --> 00:03:42,745
A printer, too.

48
00:03:42,946 --> 00:03:46,916
You have such an amazing school bag... Who are you?

49
00:03:47,417 --> 00:03:49,085
My name is Purasu Denkyoku.

50
00:03:49,285 --> 00:03:51,921
My father is the president of Super Electronic Machinery.

51
00:03:52,422 --> 00:03:57,627
What? That's the hottest company in the electronics field right now!

52
00:03:58,127 --> 00:04:00,797
So you're the heir to a huge company.

53
00:04:01,264 --> 00:04:03,166
No wonder you have amazing stuff.

54
00:04:03,633 --> 00:04:07,804
No, this super electronic school bag is still a prototype.

55
00:04:08,004 --> 00:04:10,173
I'm testing it right now.

56
00:04:10,540 --> 00:04:12,509
Does it have any other functions?

57
00:04:12,709 --> 00:04:14,143
That's a company secret.

58
00:04:14,344 --> 00:04:17,113
But I'll show you in return for showing me the map.

59
00:04:17,313 --> 00:04:19,148
All right!

60
00:04:23,319 --> 00:04:24,554
What?!

61
00:04:29,792 --> 00:04:31,194
Wow!

62
00:04:32,862 --> 00:04:36,933
I use this to record all my classes and print out photos of the notes.

63
00:04:37,533 --> 00:04:41,804
It's the world's smallest digital camera with a 48x zoom.

64
00:04:42,005 --> 00:04:43,573
This is great!

65
00:04:43,806 --> 00:04:46,709
But finding something like this makes me feel relieved.

66
00:04:46,943 --> 00:04:48,211
How nostalgic.

67
00:04:48,411 --> 00:04:50,213
That's an accessory device too.

68
00:04:50,546 --> 00:04:51,414
Huh?

69
00:04:57,320 --> 00:05:00,657
Here's the weather forecast for the Tokyo area.

70
00:05:00,857 --> 00:05:02,659
First, the sky conditions.

71
00:05:02,859 --> 00:05:06,429
Winds from the north. Later, moderately strong southwesterly winds...

72
00:05:07,063 --> 00:05:08,865
Leave making babies to me!

73
00:05:09,065 --> 00:05:09,999
This is great!

74
00:05:10,199 --> 00:05:14,070
This recorder can control all the electronic equipment.

75
00:05:15,038 --> 00:05:17,006
Music class must be quite a challenge, right?

76
00:05:17,206 --> 00:05:19,175
All sorts of switches must get activated.

77
00:05:19,375 --> 00:05:21,210
It's still a prototype.

78
00:05:22,245 --> 00:05:24,914
It's quite heavy. It feels like about five kilograms.

79
00:05:25,148 --> 00:05:26,749
That's for physical training.

80
00:05:26,983 --> 00:05:29,385
What? They even thought that far ahead?

81
00:05:29,586 --> 00:05:31,421
Hey, let me borrow it for a second!

82
00:05:31,621 --> 00:05:33,523
I can't. I'll get into trouble with my dad.

83
00:05:33,723 --> 00:05:36,359
Don't be so uptight. I'll give it back right away.

84
00:05:36,559 --> 00:05:37,760
Ryo-chan, stop.

85
00:05:37,994 --> 00:05:39,796
Just for a little while.

86
00:05:40,029 --> 00:05:40,797
Oh!

87
00:05:41,030 --> 00:05:41,731
Ah!

88
00:05:42,865 --> 00:05:44,801
My precious flowers!

89
00:05:45,034 --> 00:05:46,169
Uh-oh!

90
00:05:46,369 --> 00:05:48,204
Ryo-chan!

91
00:05:54,811 --> 00:05:57,113
What a useless airbag.

92
00:05:57,480 --> 00:05:59,382
Looks like a basic defect.

93
00:06:00,783 --> 00:06:02,785
There's room for improvement.

94
00:06:03,186 --> 00:06:04,954
Don't use me to test it!

95
00:06:05,888 --> 00:06:08,791
But still, it's an incredibly well-equipped school bag.

96
00:06:09,025 --> 00:06:10,126
We have one for adults too.

97
00:06:11,060 --> 00:06:12,061
For adults?

98
00:06:15,932 --> 00:06:18,401
It might look a little creepy.

99
00:06:18,601 --> 00:06:20,303
What are you thinking?

100
00:06:20,503 --> 00:06:24,407
The adult one isn't a school bag. It's an attaché case.

101
00:06:26,676 --> 00:06:27,677
Wow!

102
00:06:27,910 --> 00:06:30,213
It also has a communication function.

103
00:06:30,747 --> 00:06:33,416
If it had a machine gun, it'd be like 007.

104
00:06:33,616 --> 00:06:36,452
It uses a special satellite for communication.

105
00:06:36,819 --> 00:06:38,588
And if you register your fingerprint,

106
00:06:38,788 --> 00:06:41,991
it locks itself and triggers an alarm when others touch it.

107
00:06:42,458 --> 00:06:44,460
Businessmen would probably want it.

108
00:06:44,661 --> 00:06:46,462
It's due to launch after the school bag.

109
00:06:46,662 --> 00:06:50,333
We're currently recruiting people to test it for 50,000 yen a month.

110
00:06:50,633 --> 00:06:51,467
50,000 yen?

111
00:06:51,667 --> 00:06:52,869
Okay, I'll do it!

112
00:06:53,102 --> 00:06:54,137
Huh? Really?

113
00:06:54,337 --> 00:06:56,806
Sure, leave it to me!

114
00:07:02,111 --> 00:07:04,714
I haven't heard from Ryotsu at all.

115
00:07:04,947 --> 00:07:07,550
Let's leave him alone.

116
00:07:08,718 --> 00:07:09,452
Ryotsu?

117
00:07:11,788 --> 00:07:12,522
Good morning.

118
00:07:13,022 --> 00:07:14,857
What's with that yawn?

119
00:07:15,091 --> 00:07:18,194
You took three days off without permission. The chief is furious.

120
00:07:18,628 --> 00:07:19,696
What are those?

121
00:07:19,896 --> 00:07:21,664
They're the manuals for this.

122
00:07:21,864 --> 00:07:23,966
It took me three days to read them all.

123
00:07:24,267 --> 00:07:26,536
You're quite diligent outside of work.

124
00:07:26,869 --> 00:07:31,874
Now I've mastered everything from handling a digital camera to using the internet.

125
00:07:32,975 --> 00:07:34,977
I even made my own homepage.

126
00:07:35,178 --> 00:07:37,513
Wow, that's impressive in such a short time.

127
00:07:37,714 --> 00:07:38,548
Hehe.

128
00:07:38,748 --> 00:07:43,920
And I asked the president to add some new functions.

129
00:07:45,221 --> 00:07:47,457
You've gotten pretty good at it, Ryo-chan.

130
00:07:47,657 --> 00:07:48,724
Of course.

131
00:07:51,461 --> 00:07:52,829
What's that blinking dot?

132
00:07:53,229 --> 00:07:54,864
The chief's current location.

133
00:07:55,364 --> 00:07:56,065
The chief's?

134
00:07:56,299 --> 00:07:58,868
Yeah, I attached a transmitter to him.

135
00:07:59,068 --> 00:08:00,536
He's getting closer.

136
00:08:00,737 --> 00:08:02,772
From his speed, he must be in a car.

137
00:08:04,240 --> 00:08:04,907
What's this?

138
00:08:05,141 --> 00:08:07,543
When he's within 500 meters, an alarm goes off.

139
00:08:07,743 --> 00:08:10,046
Uh-oh, I've got to go.

140
00:08:10,613 --> 00:08:12,315
I'll go test this. See you later!

141
00:08:12,515 --> 00:08:13,683
Oh, Ryotsu!

142
00:08:15,251 --> 00:08:15,952
Ryotsu!

143
00:08:16,385 --> 00:08:18,054
The chief really came.

144
00:08:18,488 --> 00:08:20,223
Good morning, Chief.

145
00:08:21,390 --> 00:08:22,391
Good morning.

146
00:08:22,592 --> 00:08:24,393
Ryotsu better be here today.

147
00:08:24,594 --> 00:08:25,228
Well...

148
00:08:25,862 --> 00:08:27,597
What? Testing?

149
00:08:27,797 --> 00:08:30,967
That fool is gonna skip his health checkup again!

150
00:08:31,200 --> 00:08:32,435
His health checkup?

151
00:08:32,635 --> 00:08:37,039
Ryotsu hasn't had one for 15 years.

152
00:08:37,240 --> 00:08:38,107
So long?

153
00:08:38,341 --> 00:08:42,245
The superintendent scolded me again for poor supervision this morning.

154
00:08:42,645 --> 00:08:48,117
I've just staked my job on getting him to have his health checkup.

155
00:08:49,452 --> 00:08:51,053
You didn't have to go that far.

156
00:08:51,254 --> 00:08:53,189
Anyway, find Ryotsu!

157
00:08:53,389 --> 00:08:56,125
That's impossible. He's like a human bullet.

158
00:08:56,359 --> 00:08:59,362
Hmm, is there any way to find him?

159
00:08:59,562 --> 00:09:01,597
If this continues, I'll lose my job.

160
00:09:01,797 --> 00:09:04,000
I know! Let's call Purasu-kun!

161
00:09:08,471 --> 00:09:10,106
Step right up, step right up!

162
00:09:10,306 --> 00:09:14,143
You can watch a movie that's currently in theaters in your own home!

163
00:09:14,377 --> 00:09:16,145
And it's only 1,000 yen.

164
00:09:16,379 --> 00:09:18,114
Come on, buy one!

165
00:09:18,314 --> 00:09:20,583
-Give me one! -Me, too!

166
00:09:25,955 --> 00:09:28,825
This is a magic money tree... no, a magic money bag!

167
00:09:29,025 --> 00:09:30,126
Oh, a phone call.

168
00:09:30,326 --> 00:09:32,628
Is it the president of Super Electronic?

169
00:09:32,828 --> 00:09:33,930
Hello?

170
00:09:34,230 --> 00:09:39,235
Hey! Ryotsu! Don't take days off without permission!

171
00:09:39,836 --> 00:09:42,839
Ch-Chief, why do you know this number?

172
00:09:43,439 --> 00:09:45,308
I know everything about you!

173
00:09:45,508 --> 00:09:48,344
Ryotsu, get your health checkup today!

174
00:09:48,678 --> 00:09:50,146
Get back here right away!

175
00:09:50,346 --> 00:09:52,348
Ugh, you're so annoying...

176
00:09:55,418 --> 00:09:56,819
He hung up.

177
00:09:57,253 --> 00:10:00,957
Purasu-kun, is there any other way to find him?

178
00:10:01,157 --> 00:10:04,961
You said he attached a transmitter to you, right?

179
00:10:05,328 --> 00:10:07,964
I think I can trace him from the frequency.

180
00:10:08,364 --> 00:10:10,132
Okay, let's find the transmitter.

181
00:10:10,333 --> 00:10:12,668
It must be somewhere on your body, Chief.

182
00:10:12,868 --> 00:10:14,904
Darn it. When did he do that?

183
00:10:15,137 --> 00:10:17,807
All right, where is it? Where?

184
00:10:18,007 --> 00:10:20,176
It's not here. Not here...

185
00:10:20,376 --> 00:10:21,143
Ah!

186
00:10:21,344 --> 00:10:23,646
Oh no. Sorry, sorry.

187
00:10:23,846 --> 00:10:25,147
N-No, it's fine...

188
00:10:25,381 --> 00:10:28,050
Is there any other way to make money off this?

189
00:10:28,284 --> 00:10:29,485
You're fired!

190
00:10:30,386 --> 00:10:32,154
Chief! I'm sorry! Huh?

191
00:10:32,355 --> 00:10:33,289
What are you doing!

192
00:10:33,489 --> 00:10:34,290
Please spare me.

193
00:10:34,490 --> 00:10:35,625
Oh, it wasn't me.

194
00:10:35,825 --> 00:10:37,827
I'll lose hundreds of millions in profits!

195
00:10:38,628 --> 00:10:39,829
Hundreds of millions?

196
00:10:40,563 --> 00:10:41,931
Hey, what's wrong?

197
00:10:42,164 --> 00:10:45,067
The computer in my car broke down,

198
00:10:45,301 --> 00:10:48,471
and I can't access important information.

199
00:10:49,238 --> 00:10:53,542
I can use my Super Electronic GX767 for computer communication.

200
00:10:53,743 --> 00:10:54,577
Are you sure?

201
00:10:54,777 --> 00:10:55,478
Yes!

202
00:10:58,514 --> 00:10:59,415
Oh!

203
00:10:59,882 --> 00:11:03,519
But the access fee is high.

204
00:11:03,719 --> 00:11:07,323
Looks like you can make a lot of money, so I have to get 10% of the profits.

205
00:11:08,124 --> 00:11:10,092
That's too high. How about 1%?

206
00:11:10,760 --> 00:11:13,796
I have no choice. How about 7% in the middle?

207
00:11:14,030 --> 00:11:15,364
That's not the middle!

208
00:11:15,665 --> 00:11:17,099
If you don't like it, that's fine.

209
00:11:17,500 --> 00:11:20,870
Hmm, okay. I'll settle for 7%.

210
00:11:21,070 --> 00:11:22,905
All right, it's a deal.

211
00:11:23,806 --> 00:11:25,775
Hurry up. The White House.

212
00:11:25,975 --> 00:11:27,443
At exactly 5 p.m. Japan time,

213
00:11:27,677 --> 00:11:30,513
the government purchase price for oranges will be announced.

214
00:11:30,713 --> 00:11:31,948
I want to know it.

215
00:11:32,248 --> 00:11:34,450
We don't have much time. What's the address?

216
00:11:35,051 --> 00:11:35,985
Here it is.

217
00:11:36,218 --> 00:11:37,219
Password?

218
00:11:37,620 --> 00:11:38,287
Okay.

219
00:11:41,957 --> 00:11:42,892
That's pretty fast.

220
00:11:43,092 --> 00:11:45,561
It's using a special satellite for communication.

221
00:11:46,295 --> 00:11:48,164
Oh, here's the price of oranges.

222
00:11:48,397 --> 00:11:49,565
It's higher than last year.

223
00:11:50,366 --> 00:11:53,736
Hey, call head office and buy up all orange-related stocks in the world.

224
00:11:53,936 --> 00:11:54,837
Yes, sir.

225
00:11:59,008 --> 00:12:00,710
Sorry, sir. My battery's dead.

226
00:12:00,910 --> 00:12:01,911
You idiot!

227
00:12:02,111 --> 00:12:05,481
Use my phone. It's a private line, so it'll get through right away.

228
00:12:05,715 --> 00:12:07,016
Oh, thank you!

229
00:12:09,285 --> 00:12:10,286
I found it!

230
00:12:10,820 --> 00:12:13,122
That jerk, this is out of spite for his bonus.

231
00:12:13,322 --> 00:12:15,591
Can I borrow it? I'll connect it now.

232
00:12:16,192 --> 00:12:21,630
Ryotsu! I'll find you and make sure you get a health checkup!

233
00:12:34,477 --> 00:12:39,515
Wow! Orange-related stocks have doubled on the Singapore Exchange!

234
00:12:39,815 --> 00:12:42,018
Good, good, Mr. Ryotsu!

235
00:12:42,284 --> 00:12:44,987
The London stock market is about to open soon.

236
00:12:45,521 --> 00:12:46,655
Access it.

237
00:12:46,856 --> 00:12:47,690
Roger that.

238
00:12:48,224 --> 00:12:49,191
Oh, here it is.

239
00:12:49,658 --> 00:12:53,696
Orange stocks... Oh, they've doubled just after trading started!

240
00:12:53,963 --> 00:12:55,331
Okay, sell them all!

241
00:12:55,531 --> 00:12:58,234
You fool! We can't play a bad card like a two!

242
00:12:58,467 --> 00:13:01,070
This is stock trading, not Japanese baccarat.

243
00:13:01,771 --> 00:13:05,374
They're basically the same. Just wait until they triple.

244
00:13:05,608 --> 00:13:07,209
We can't go that far...

245
00:13:12,014 --> 00:13:15,217
Mmm, delicious. But it's quite extravagant.

246
00:13:15,451 --> 00:13:18,521
Thanks to you, I've made about 300 million. Thank you.

247
00:13:18,721 --> 00:13:20,723
300 million yen, huh? That's good.

248
00:13:20,923 --> 00:13:22,858
No, no, it's 300 million dollars.

249
00:13:23,059 --> 00:13:25,728
Dollars? If it's 110 yen to the dollar...

250
00:13:25,928 --> 00:13:28,464
That's 33 billion yen!

251
00:13:28,664 --> 00:13:31,167
Yes. Now here's your share.

252
00:13:31,367 --> 00:13:33,536
It was 7%, right?

253
00:13:33,736 --> 00:13:36,472
What? One, ten, hundred...

254
00:13:36,672 --> 00:13:39,475
2.31 billion yen?

255
00:13:40,376 --> 00:13:43,712
2.31 billion yen!

256
00:13:44,547 --> 00:13:46,482
Is it okay for me to get this much?

257
00:13:46,682 --> 00:13:48,951
Yes! It was a promise.

258
00:13:49,185 --> 00:13:51,821
More importantly, you have a talent for business.

259
00:13:52,021 --> 00:13:54,423
Would you be my partner?

260
00:13:54,657 --> 00:13:55,491
Partner?

261
00:13:56,125 --> 00:13:59,061
How about an annual salary of one billion yen?

262
00:13:59,829 --> 00:14:01,564
One billion yen?

263
00:14:02,298 --> 00:14:03,232
Are you unhappy?

264
00:14:03,432 --> 00:14:06,302
No, no. Okay, okay!

265
00:14:12,908 --> 00:14:14,310
"ROBERT & RYOTSU COMPANY"

266
00:14:22,418 --> 00:14:24,086
Good morning, sir.

267
00:14:24,286 --> 00:14:25,688
Yeah, good morning.

268
00:14:28,924 --> 00:14:30,126
Good morning, sir.

269
00:14:30,326 --> 00:14:30,993
Good morning.

270
00:14:31,227 --> 00:14:33,229
Good morning, sir.

271
00:14:33,863 --> 00:14:34,730
Good morning.

272
00:14:34,930 --> 00:14:36,899
Good morning, sir.

273
00:14:39,068 --> 00:14:41,570
How's the vice president's chair?

274
00:14:41,770 --> 00:14:43,806
Oh, not bad.

275
00:14:44,340 --> 00:14:45,174
Bad news!

276
00:14:45,407 --> 00:14:49,311
A cold wave hit Ukraine causing devastating damage to wheat.

277
00:14:49,545 --> 00:14:50,479
What?

278
00:14:52,715 --> 00:14:55,651
U.S. wheat prices are soaring.

279
00:14:56,118 --> 00:14:59,955
I guess other investors have already secured American wheat.

280
00:15:00,156 --> 00:15:02,725
Okay, let's buy up Australian wheat!

281
00:15:02,925 --> 00:15:04,660
Hold on. A phone won't do.

282
00:15:04,894 --> 00:15:06,996
In times like this, cash talks.

283
00:15:07,263 --> 00:15:09,732
We go straight to the farmers and make the deal in person.

284
00:15:10,299 --> 00:15:11,367
I see.

285
00:15:12,034 --> 00:15:15,838
Vice President, will you fly to Australia with me?

286
00:15:16,038 --> 00:15:17,373
You bet I will!

287
00:15:18,107 --> 00:15:20,309
I've got my private plane waiting at Haneda.

288
00:15:20,509 --> 00:15:22,011
We'll head straight there in this.

289
00:15:22,211 --> 00:15:24,747
Only executives could pull this off!

290
00:15:27,783 --> 00:15:30,319
Looks like Ryotsu-san's heading to Haneda Airport.

291
00:15:30,519 --> 00:15:33,155
Damn him. He's trying to run away.

292
00:15:33,622 --> 00:15:34,957
Hokkaido? Kyushu?

293
00:15:35,157 --> 00:15:36,292
I have no idea.

294
00:15:39,962 --> 00:15:40,930
He's on that plane!

295
00:15:41,130 --> 00:15:41,931
Hmm? Oh!

296
00:15:42,932 --> 00:15:44,166
Overseas?!

297
00:15:53,008 --> 00:15:55,010
Chief, what are you going to do?

298
00:15:55,211 --> 00:15:57,012
My job is at stake!

299
00:15:57,212 --> 00:15:59,949
I'll make him get a health checkup no matter what!

300
00:16:00,249 --> 00:16:02,651
I won't let you get away, Ryotsu!

301
00:16:02,851 --> 00:16:05,888
Chief, leave the flight arrangements to me.

302
00:16:09,725 --> 00:16:13,162
I'm sure this SR-71 can catch up.

303
00:16:27,109 --> 00:16:28,844
Hmm.

304
00:16:29,445 --> 00:16:30,713
He's pretty tough.

305
00:16:30,913 --> 00:16:32,114
That sly old fox!

306
00:16:33,015 --> 00:16:34,550
What is it? I'm busy now.

307
00:16:35,551 --> 00:16:36,385
Hello?

308
00:16:36,585 --> 00:16:40,256
Ryotsu! What are you doing in Australia?

309
00:16:40,456 --> 00:16:42,057
Chief! How did you know?

310
00:16:42,257 --> 00:16:46,428
Ryotsu-san, I didn't ask you to go overseas to test it.

311
00:16:46,662 --> 00:16:47,296
Gah!

312
00:16:47,696 --> 00:16:48,530
What's wrong?

313
00:16:48,731 --> 00:16:50,099
N-Nothing.

314
00:16:50,299 --> 00:16:53,869
I'm in the middle of an important business negotiation.

315
00:16:55,237 --> 00:16:56,071
Huh?

316
00:16:58,007 --> 00:16:58,674
Oh!

317
00:17:01,143 --> 00:17:04,446
Ryotsu! Come out!

318
00:17:04,680 --> 00:17:07,249
Go back to Japan right away and get a health checkup!

319
00:17:09,485 --> 00:17:11,720
Vice President, what is that?

320
00:17:11,920 --> 00:17:13,722
Damn Nakagawa!

321
00:17:13,922 --> 00:17:17,059
I'm not gonna get caught here. Let's close the deal quickly.

322
00:17:17,426 --> 00:17:20,062
Come on, take it, thief! Here we go!

323
00:17:23,799 --> 00:17:25,801
That was a great decision.

324
00:17:26,035 --> 00:17:26,902
Oh, yes...

325
00:17:27,102 --> 00:17:30,239
Argh! Can't you go any faster?

326
00:17:30,873 --> 00:17:31,874
No more than this...

327
00:17:32,074 --> 00:17:34,977
Come on, show some guts!

328
00:17:35,177 --> 00:17:36,512
Ryotsu!

329
00:17:36,945 --> 00:17:38,747
You can't run away anywhere!

330
00:17:39,314 --> 00:17:41,750
We have a super school bag here!

331
00:17:42,818 --> 00:17:46,822
I have a super attaché case here too!

332
00:17:47,056 --> 00:17:47,890
I won't lose!

333
00:17:48,424 --> 00:17:51,894
Stop doing stupid things and come back with us to get a health checkup!

334
00:17:52,361 --> 00:17:54,330
I quit being a cop

335
00:17:54,530 --> 00:17:57,733
and became a vice president with an annual salary of a billion yen!

336
00:17:58,167 --> 00:18:01,470
I don't need to have a police health checkup anymore.

337
00:18:01,670 --> 00:18:04,173
What are you talking about?

338
00:18:04,640 --> 00:18:10,179
I live in a different world from you common folks now, Chief! Goodbye!

339
00:18:12,348 --> 00:18:13,849
Don't give me "goodbye"!

340
00:18:14,083 --> 00:18:16,352
Nakagawa, can't you fire a warning shot?

341
00:18:16,852 --> 00:18:18,354
This helicopter isn't armed.

342
00:18:18,754 --> 00:18:20,089
Purasu-kun, you got anything?

343
00:18:20,289 --> 00:18:22,524
There's a signal flare attached to my school bag.

344
00:18:22,758 --> 00:18:23,559
Oh, I see.

345
00:18:23,959 --> 00:18:25,361
You even have one of those?

346
00:18:25,828 --> 00:18:26,929
It's for self-defense.

347
00:18:27,129 --> 00:18:28,363
Okay, that'll do.

348
00:18:31,233 --> 00:18:32,768
They're so persistent!

349
00:18:33,235 --> 00:18:34,503
Okay, Purasu-kun!

350
00:18:35,204 --> 00:18:37,005
W-What are you gonna do?

351
00:18:37,206 --> 00:18:38,407
Here we go!

352
00:18:40,008 --> 00:18:42,511
-Whoa! -Oh no!

353
00:18:43,145 --> 00:18:44,313
W-What's going on?

354
00:18:44,513 --> 00:18:46,548
Damn it, if that's the way you want it...

355
00:18:46,782 --> 00:18:48,484
There's a missile in that school bag.

356
00:18:48,684 --> 00:18:51,019
There must be a weapon in this attaché case, too.

357
00:18:51,220 --> 00:18:52,521
Oh, there it is!

358
00:18:53,021 --> 00:18:53,889
All right!

359
00:18:56,425 --> 00:18:57,226
Oh?!

360
00:18:57,826 --> 00:18:59,194
Hmm? Ah!

361
00:18:59,394 --> 00:19:01,897
Argh!

362
00:19:02,664 --> 00:19:03,732
Ryotsu!

363
00:19:04,133 --> 00:19:05,734
Oh no!

364
00:19:07,236 --> 00:19:08,537
You've dug your own grave!

365
00:19:08,737 --> 00:19:11,206
Nakagawa, deport him back to Japan like this.

366
00:19:11,407 --> 00:19:12,241
Yes, sir!

367
00:19:16,078 --> 00:19:17,379
Ryotsu!

368
00:19:17,813 --> 00:19:19,381
Damn it!

369
00:19:19,748 --> 00:19:20,582
Oh?

370
00:19:20,816 --> 00:19:23,085
What's this button?

371
00:19:24,620 --> 00:19:25,454
Argh!

372
00:19:28,891 --> 00:19:29,725
Ryo-chan!

373
00:19:39,635 --> 00:19:43,105
Justice always wins. So long!

374
00:19:43,439 --> 00:19:46,108
Grr... That damn lucky jerk!

375
00:19:46,308 --> 00:19:49,945
Purasu-kun, is there any other way to catch Ryo-chan?

376
00:19:50,179 --> 00:19:52,781
I can track him down, but catching him...

377
00:19:53,415 --> 00:19:55,784
How about calling again and persuading him?

378
00:19:56,285 --> 00:19:57,386
It's no use.

379
00:19:57,586 --> 00:19:59,388
Oh, I have a good idea.

380
00:19:59,588 --> 00:20:00,255
What?

381
00:20:06,094 --> 00:20:09,031
Hey! This isn't a show!

382
00:20:11,066 --> 00:20:13,302
Oh, brother! Over here!

383
00:20:14,136 --> 00:20:16,471
Ryotsu, this is no time for that!

384
00:20:16,672 --> 00:20:18,607
The gold market price is falling!

385
00:20:18,807 --> 00:20:22,044
Sell all the gold our company has right now!

386
00:20:22,244 --> 00:20:23,245
Got it!

387
00:20:24,346 --> 00:20:25,080
Hurry, Ryotsu!

388
00:20:25,280 --> 00:20:26,682
No need to panic.

389
00:20:27,483 --> 00:20:29,818
That's weird. I can't get access.

390
00:20:30,486 --> 00:20:31,487
What are you doing?

391
00:20:31,687 --> 00:20:33,889
If you don't act fast, we'll suffer huge losses!

392
00:20:34,289 --> 00:20:36,892
Be that as it may, something's weird.

393
00:20:37,793 --> 00:20:42,130
Oh no! We're losing 50 million dollars every second!

394
00:20:42,764 --> 00:20:44,066
Hurry up, Ryotsu!

395
00:20:44,266 --> 00:20:45,367
I know!

396
00:20:46,268 --> 00:20:49,471
It was receiving a fax. No wonder it couldn't connect.

397
00:20:50,138 --> 00:20:52,474
Who is sending it in this emergency?

398
00:20:53,275 --> 00:20:54,977
Th-The chief!

399
00:20:55,444 --> 00:20:57,613
Ryotsu! What are you doing?

400
00:20:57,813 --> 00:20:59,982
If this continues, our company will go bankrupt!

401
00:21:00,349 --> 00:21:02,718
I'll stop the fax right now.

402
00:21:02,951 --> 00:21:05,621
Well, the switch is... inside.

403
00:21:06,321 --> 00:21:07,189
What?

404
00:21:07,956 --> 00:21:09,691
Damn, it's locked!

405
00:21:09,925 --> 00:21:13,195
We're already in the red by $1.02 billion, Ryotsu!

406
00:21:13,662 --> 00:21:15,130
It's sound-activated.

407
00:21:15,564 --> 00:21:17,399
I'll have to open it with the recorder.

408
00:21:17,633 --> 00:21:19,935
I think it was do-mi-so.

409
00:21:22,804 --> 00:21:23,472
Huh?

410
00:21:23,672 --> 00:21:25,474
Ryotsu!

411
00:21:25,674 --> 00:21:28,110
Was it do-fa-la?

412
00:21:32,147 --> 00:21:32,981
Oh...

413
00:21:35,217 --> 00:21:37,219
Bravo!

414
00:21:39,488 --> 00:21:40,589
No!

415
00:21:41,690 --> 00:21:42,691
It stopped somehow.

416
00:21:43,525 --> 00:21:44,192
Eeek!

417
00:21:45,027 --> 00:21:46,562
What the heck? Shut up!

418
00:21:46,762 --> 00:21:49,164
Two Chinese rice bowls and one ramen rice, please.

419
00:21:49,498 --> 00:21:50,766
Cut the crap!

420
00:21:51,533 --> 00:21:52,901
Oops, it'll be bad if it breaks.

421
00:21:54,403 --> 00:21:57,072
Thief! Thief! Thief!

422
00:21:57,306 --> 00:22:00,075
What are you doing! Sell the gold quickly!

423
00:22:00,309 --> 00:22:01,610
I know.

424
00:22:01,843 --> 00:22:04,212
Looks like it broke from the shock just now.

425
00:22:04,413 --> 00:22:06,081
Hey, I'm the owner! Hey!

426
00:22:07,883 --> 00:22:09,918
Whoa, ouch, ouch! Stop! Let me go!

427
00:22:10,152 --> 00:22:11,353
I'm the owner, Ryotsu!

428
00:22:11,553 --> 00:22:13,221
Fingerprints do not match.

429
00:22:13,422 --> 00:22:15,223
I told you it's me!

430
00:22:15,557 --> 00:22:16,391
Ryotsu!

431
00:22:17,726 --> 00:22:20,929
To protect classified data, self-destructing in 60 seconds.

432
00:22:21,163 --> 00:22:21,763
What?!

433
00:22:21,997 --> 00:22:23,599
59, 58...

434
00:22:23,799 --> 00:22:25,267
You've gotta be kidding me!

435
00:22:25,467 --> 00:22:27,336
Ryotsu! Damn you...

436
00:22:27,536 --> 00:22:28,770
No time for that!

437
00:22:29,004 --> 00:22:32,107
At this rate, this is gonna blow the whole cruise ship to bits!

438
00:22:32,341 --> 00:22:33,275
50 seconds left.

439
00:22:34,643 --> 00:22:36,044
Mr. Ryotsu.

440
00:22:36,545 --> 00:22:39,915
You have quite a unique business sense.

441
00:22:40,115 --> 00:22:43,552
R-Really? I've always thought so.

442
00:22:43,752 --> 00:22:47,589
I saw it in you at a glance, and I have a good sense too, right?

443
00:22:48,423 --> 00:22:49,358
But...

444
00:22:49,558 --> 00:22:51,727
Oh! My check!

445
00:22:52,661 --> 00:22:54,663
I guess I was totally blind!

446
00:22:54,896 --> 00:22:56,631
You're fired!

447
00:22:56,832 --> 00:22:58,133
No way!

448
00:22:59,635 --> 00:23:03,472
I'm going to use this to cover the losses you caused.

449
00:23:04,406 --> 00:23:06,908
3, 2, 1.

450
00:23:13,482 --> 00:23:16,051
It seems the data protection system was activated.

451
00:23:16,585 --> 00:23:17,486
Oh! Over there!

452
00:23:27,162 --> 00:23:30,699
What a damn lucky idiot to survive that explosion!

453
00:23:30,932 --> 00:23:35,671
Not enough explosive, and the safety airbag went off, too.

454
00:23:35,871 --> 00:23:38,840
I'll report this to my father for improvement.

455
00:23:39,074 --> 00:23:42,844
I'll have a health checkup or whatever, so please help me!

456
00:23:43,445 --> 00:23:46,114
Huh? Didn't you quit being a cop, Ryotsu?

457
00:23:46,314 --> 00:23:47,883
No need to do it anymore!

458
00:23:48,116 --> 00:23:50,085
Thank you for being a tester.

459
00:23:50,285 --> 00:23:52,254
I'll transfer the fee to your account.

460
00:23:52,454 --> 00:23:54,122
Okay, everyone, let's go home.

461
00:23:54,322 --> 00:23:55,157
Yes, sir!

462
00:23:56,191 --> 00:23:57,459
Hey, wait a minute!

463
00:23:57,659 --> 00:23:59,261
That was a joke!

464
00:23:59,461 --> 00:24:00,729
You're too cold!

465
00:24:00,962 --> 00:24:02,431
Where's your humanity?

466
00:24:03,098 --> 00:24:08,904
TEARS IN THE CHIEF'S EYES
